gh\ncores/bench/rtl/alu.sv:29:  // half). Verilator's UNUSEDSIGNAL is silenced locally — the unused\ncores/bench/rtl/alu.sv:30:  // bits are dead-code-eliminated by Yosys.\ncores/bench/rtl/alu.sv:32:  logic signed [63:0] mul_ss;  // signed*signed\ncores/bench/rtl/alu.sv:33:  logic        [63:0] mul_uu;  // unsigned*unsigned (both halves used)\ncores/bench/rtl/alu.sv:34:  logic signed [63:0] mul_su;  // signed*unsigned (a signed, b unsigned)\ncores/bench/rtl/alu.sv:57:      // M-extension. Under RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS the hardware operations\ncores/bench/rtl/alu.sv:58:      // are substituted for tractable algebraic stand-ins so bitwuzla\ncores/bench/rtl/alu.sv:59:      // can solve the BMC inside the 20-step depth budget. The same\ncores/bench/rtl/alu.sv:60:      // substitution must appear in the riscv-formal spec (insn_*.v).\ncores/bench/rtl/alu.sv:61:      // The Verilator/cocotb/cosim builds leave ALTOPS undefined and\ncores/bench/rtl/alu.sv:62:      // run the real arithmetic.\ncores/bench/rtl/alu.sv:77:      // Divide and remainder share the EX-stage iterative divider. Its\ncores/bench/rtl/alu.sv:78:      // result is held until this operation is accepted into EX/MEM.\n cores/bench/rtl/alu.sv         | 22 +++---------\n cores/bench/rtl/core.sv        |  5 ++-\n cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv    | 76 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-----\n cores/bench/rtl/hazard_unit.sv |  7 ++--\n cores/bench/test/test_alu.py   | 15 ++++++---\n 5 files changed, 90 insertions(+), 35 deletions(-)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
