{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_41","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"git check-ignore -v cores/bench/implementation_notes.md || true; sed -n '1,180p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md; git diff --check; git status --short\"","aggregated_output":".gitignore:87:cores/*/implementation_notes.md\tcores/bench/implementation_notes.md\n# Iterative divider implementation\n\n## Changes\n\n- Added `rtl/iterative_divider.sv`, a shared 32-step radix-2 restoring divider for DIV, DIVU, REM, and REMU. Signed operands are converted to magnitudes, with sign restoration and explicit divide-by-zero results.\n- Removed combinational `/` and `%` from `alu.sv`; EX supplies the divider's held result.\n- Added an EX completion handshake. ID/EX and fetch wait during division, EX/MEM receives bubbles until completion, and the result retires once. Existing data-memory stall priority is preserved.\n- Snapshot forwarded divide operands at request time so RVFI records the operands actually consumed even after forwarding sources drain.\n- Kept the RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS build single-cycle, using the existing matching M-extension stand-ins. Added cycle-level divider tests for arithmetic, corner cases, latency, and result holding.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Ordered RTL lint: `make lint TARGET=bench` passed.\n- Divider and ALU cocotb tests: `pytest -q cores/bench/test/test_divider.py cores/bench/test/test_alu.py` passed (2 test runners).\n- Formal: `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh` passed all 53 checks with the nret=1 wrapper.\n- Cosim: `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench` passed selftest and CoreMark CRC validation with bus stalls.\n- Gowin timing: placement option 0 reported 44.016 MHz. Its worst path is now regfile read through ID/EX, EX/IF/hazard, back to ID/EX (28.013 ns, 23 logic levels); it no longer crosses a combinational divider.\n\n## Notes and concerns\n\n- The literal lint command with `rtl/*.sv` sorts `core_pkg.sv` after dependent modules and fails the repo's documented source-order requirement. The Makefile lint target places `core_pkg.sv` first and passes.\n- The first direct `make cosim` build defaulted to NRET=2 although this core declares NRET=1. Re-running with `NRET=1`, matching the evaluator's `core.yaml` configuration, passed.\n- Formal uses ALTOPS and therefore checks the interlock in its single-cycle abstraction; real divider arithmetic and end-to-end behavior were exercised by cocotb and stalled cosim. The measured timing is from one Gowin placement option; it is not a three-placement median.\n M cores/bench/rtl/alu.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/core.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n M cores/bench/test/test_alu.py\n?? cores/bench/rtl/iterative_divider.sv\n?? cores/bench/test/test_divider.py\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
