{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_57","type":"agent_message","text":"The retry exposed a second form of the same stale-entry issue: a reserved branch encoding has the branch opcode, but decode marks it illegal, so an opcode-only fetch check still predicts it. I’m moving the final correction into EX: compare the predicted next PC with the instruction’s fully resolved next PC for every valid instruction. This also handles stale entries for jumps and illegal instructions while keeping instruction decode out of fetch."}}
