D namespace where $$ is 2 or 3\n# for every agent, so siblings wrote into one dir and wiped each other's\n# checks mid-SBY (V2 incident 03). mktemp gives a unique name instead.\n# FORMAL_WORK_ID pins the suffix so tools/eval/formal.py can remove exactly\n# its own dir afterwards. genchecks.py derives @core\n…[5279 of 8351 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:b64fb124be803c69]…\nglob, with core_pkg.sv first and wrapper.sv last.\nSTAGED_CFG=\"$CORE_DIR/checks.cfg\"\nawk '/^\\[verilog-files\\]/{exit} {print}' \"$CHECKS_CFG\" > \"$STAGED_CFG\"\n{\n    echo \"[verilog-files]\"\n    [ -f \"$CORE_DIR/core_pkg.sv\" ] && \\\n        echo \"@basedir@/cores/@core@/core_pkg.sv\"\n    for f in \"$CORE_DIR\"/*.sv; do\n        name=\"$(basename \"$f\")\"\n        [ \"$name\" = \"core_pkg.sv\" ] && continue\n        [ \"$name\" = \"wrapper.sv\" ] && continue\n        echo \"@basedir@/cores/@core@/$name\"\nname: bench\ndescription: Frozen LLM-benchmark fixture core. Identical RTL to baseline at the bench-fixture-v1\n  freeze point. The benchmark matrix clones from the bench-fixture-v1 orphan branch\n  and operates only on this directory.\nisa: rv32im\nnret: 1\ntarget_fpga: tang-nano-20k\ntargets:\n  fmax_mhz: 135\n  lut4: 10000\n  coremark_iter_s: 300\n  coremark_per_mhz: 2.2\ncurrent:\n  fmax_mhz: 49.862\n  lut4: 3762\n  ff: 1605\n  coremark_iter_s: 2.0e-06\n  coremark_per_mhz: 0.0\n  source_id: hyp-20260930-001-r2s0\n  updated: '2026-09-30T20:12:47.259825Z'\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
