{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_31","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"git status --short && git diff --stat && git diff --check && sed -n '1,180p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md && git -C formal/riscv-formal status --short | head -20\"","aggregated_output":" M cores/bench/rtl/core.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n cores/bench/rtl/core.sv        | 20 ++++++++++++++++--\n cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv    | 48 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-----\n cores/bench/rtl/hazard_unit.sv | 12 +++++++++--\n 3 files changed, 71 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)\n# Register control-transfer recovery\n\n## Changes\n\n- EX now captures a resolved branch misprediction or valid jump target in a\n  one-entry recovery register. Predictor updates still occur when the branch\n  is accepted, and a pending target stays stable until recovery is accepted.\n- IF consumes the registered request through its existing redirect input. Its\n  redirect priority updates the PC even during an instruction-memory stall;\n  the fetch payload is invalidated for that cycle.\n- Hazard control defers recovery acceptance during a data-memory stall and\n  flushes ID when it can consume the request. Core masks the wrong-path ID/EX\n  controls and valid bit while recovery is pending so it cannot initiate a\n  store, load, multiply, or divide before the flush edge.\n\n## Deviations and concerns\n\nIF's existing redirect handling already supported a held PC update and an\ninvalid fetch payload, so no IF RTL change was needed. Recovery adds a cycle\nfor predictor misses and jumps; correct predicted branches remain on the\nexisting fast path. Timing still reports the forwarded EX/ALU to data-memory\noutput path as critical, at 64.446 MHz for placement option 0.\n\n## Local checks\n\n- Verilator lint: pass.\n- `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh`: 53 passed,\n  0 failed.\n- `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`: pass, both