Outputs:\n-//   stall_if / stall_id : freeze the PC reg and the IF/ID combinational\n-//                          payload (cleared by ID's flush input).\n-//   flush_if / flush_id : on EX redirect, kill the two in-flight\n-//                          instructions ahead of the redirect target.\n-//   flush_id       \n…[3024 of 6096 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:01ac1019d4e39ebf]…\nl/if_stage.sv\n+++ b/cores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv\n@@ -5,10 +5,9 @@\n // flop in this microarchitecture, the next-stage's ID/EX register\n // captures everything one cycle later.\n //\n-// On flush or redirect, the instruction emitted to ID is forced to NOP\n-// (`0x00000013` = ADDI x0,x0,0). This prevents the hazard unit from\n-// observing a real rs1/rs2 from a wrong-path instruction and inserting\n-// a spurious load-use stall the cycle after a taken branch.\n+// The instruction payload always reflects imem_data. Redirects and\n+// unavailable fetches are represented only by `valid`, keeping redirect\n+// control off the 32-bit instruction/decode path.\n //\n // Latency:        PC-reg update is synchronous; output is combinational.\n // RVFI fields:    feeds pc_rdata (via ID/EX/MEM/WB) and pc_wdata (via\n@@ -50,7 +49,7 @@ module if_stage (\n \n   always_comb begin\n     out.pc    = pc;\n-    out.instr = (flush || redirect) ? 32'h0000_0013 : imem_data;\n+    out.instr = imem_data;\n     out.valid = !(flush || redirect);\n   end\n \n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_36","type":"agent_message","text":"Implemented valid-bit fetch bubbles in [if_stage.sv](/srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6-luna_xhigh-v2-rep5/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261001-002-r7s1/cores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv), [id_stage.sv](/srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6-luna_xhigh-v2-rep5/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261001-002-r7s1/cores/bench/rtl/id_stage.sv), [hazard_unit.sv](/srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6-luna_xhigh-v2-rep5/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261001-002-r7s1/cores/bench/rtl/hazard_unit.sv), and [core.sv](/srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6-luna_xhigh-v2-rep5/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261001-002-r7s1/cores/bench/rtl/core.sv). Fetch payload now passes through unchanged; invalid entries become side-effect-free ID bubbles, and load-use detection checks IF/ID validity.\n\n**Checks:** Verilator lint passed; formal passed (53 checks, 0 failures); cosim passed both ELF tests with `NRET=1`. The plain cosim command defaults to `NRET=2` and fails to compile against this core’s `nret: 1` interface. Gowin Fmax across three placement options was **53.246 MHz median**; the worst paths now run through forwarding and EX to the data-memory outputs.\n\nImplementation details and check results are in [implementation_notes.md](/srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6-luna_xhigh-v2-rep5/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261001-002-r7s1/cores/bench/implementation_notes.md)."}}
