{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"git status --short && test -f cores/bench/implementation_notes.md && sed -n '1,80p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md && git diff --check\"","aggregated_output":" M cores/bench/rtl/core.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv\n# Implementation notes\n\n## Changes\n\n- Split the IF direction predictor into eight-entry backward and forward banks.\n- Initialize backward counters to `2'b10` (weakly taken) and forward counters to `2'b01` (weakly not-taken).\n- Select a bank at fetch with the branch immediate sign and `PC[4:2]`.\n- Widened the predictor update index to four bits and carry `{resolved_imm[31], resolved_pc[4:2]}` from EX through `core`, so training updates the same branch class and PC slot used at lookup.\n\nNo test files or other RTL modules needed changes.\n\n## Deviations and concerns\n\nThe implementation follows the proposed bank split directly. The larger counter state and bank selection add predictor storage and a small mux; FPGA timing and fitness have not been measured locally.\n\n## Local checks\n\n- Verilator lint: passed.\n- Formal: passed, 53 checks, 0 failed (`RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh`).\n- Cosim: passed for both ELF workloads (`NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`). The `NRET=1` environment override is needed for the manual Makefile invocation because this core has `nret: 1`; with the default `NRET=2`, the C++ harness expected absent channel-1 ports.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"agent_message","text":"Implemented separate backward and forward direction-counter banks in [if_stage.sv](/srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6-luna_xhigh-v2-rep5/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261001-003-r15s2/cores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv). EX carries the resolved displacement sign with `PC[4:2]` so training updates the matching bank.\n\nLint passed. Formal passed all 53 checks. Cosim passed for both ELF workloads with `NRET=1`; the default Make invocation uses `NRET=2`, which expects channel-1 ports absent from this nret=1 core. FPGA timing was not measured. Implementation notes are in [implementation_notes.md](/srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6-luna_xhigh-v2-rep5/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261001-003-r15s2/cores/bench/implementation_notes.md)."}}
