he resource savings.\n- 2026-09-30 hyp-20260930-003-r4s2 (regression, -3.04%): Shrinking branch prediction to one registered entry removes BTB indexing, but the 32-bit PC-tag compare and taken-target mux still burden the IF PC path, so this lookup simplification alone did not recover CoreMark fitness.\n- 2026-09-30 hyp-20260930-001-r5s0 (regression, -8.56%): On the EX-to-redirect path, one-hot forwarding replaces selector decode with per-bit masked-OR operand logic and priority suppression, whose added data gating can outweigh the removed binary mux decode.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
