{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260930-003-r5s2.yaml'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260930-003-r5s2\ntitle: \"Retimed next-PC branch prediction\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  EX-resolved taken branches discard younger work, but prior predictors added target lookup, comparison, or return selection directly to the fetch PC path and reduced Fmax. A predictor can still avoid recurring loop redirects if its lookup result is registered before that branch reaches the PC selection point.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a small tagged branch target predictor whose lookup for the next sequential PC is performed one cycle ahead and stored with that PC. The IF PC update then selects between PC+4 and the already-registered predicted target, keeping the tag comparison and target selection out of the predictor-to-PC feedback path. Carry the prediction with the instruction, train the entry on EX branch resolution, and retain redirect recovery for misses and incorrect outcomes. Repeated CoreMark loop branches should reduce redirect bubbles while the retimed lookup limits the Fmax cost that hurt earlier BTB designs.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add prediction-valid and predicted-target metadata to the fetch and execute pipeline bundles.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Register a next-PC predictor lookup one cycle ahead and use its saved result for PC selection.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Carry the prediction metadata with the fetched instruction into execute.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Train the target entry from resolved branches and recover on prediction mismatch.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Connect predictor update signals and preserve correct prediction state across stalls and redirects.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
