{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_3", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'tail -6 cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl; cat cores/bench/CORE_PHILOSOPHY.md; git status --short'", "aggregated_output": "{\"id\": \"hyp-20261001-002-r11s1\", \"title\": \"Register operands before execute\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The recent FPGA timing paths still cross the execute stage's operand and arithmetic logic before reaching a memory-side output. Forwarding selection, ALU work, and branch resolution currently share one cycle. A pipeline boundary after forwarded operand preparation can reduce the combinational work on this path while preserving one-instruction-per-cycle throughput.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The recent FPGA timing paths still cross the execute stage's operand and arithmetic logic before reaching a memory-side output. Forwarding selection, ALU work, and branch resolution currently share one cycle. A pipeline boundary after forwarded operand preparation can reduce the combinational work on this path while preserving one-instruction-per-cycle throughput.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Split execute into an operand-preparation stage and an arithmetic stage. The first stage selects the freshest forwarded source values and registers them with the instruction, PC, immediate, and control metadata; the second stage performs ALU/address generation and branch or jump resolution into EX/MEM. Add a dedicated younger-entry flush on redirects and align IF, both execute-stage valid bits, and PC-next metadata so no wrong-path instruction retires and consecutive retirement PCs remain continuous. Keep load-use, data-memory stall, divider, and multiplier interlocks aligned to the new boundary. With forwarding selection no longer serial with the ALU, the common register-to-result path should shorten; the existing direction predictor should limit the added branch-resolution cost.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 7, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add an operand-stage payload carrying forwarded values and the instruction metadata needed by execute and retirement.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Register forwarded operands before arithmetic, then reso\n…[19320 of 22392 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:4cff4a6456fa6d22]…\nlta_pct\": -13.31, \"vs_baseline\": 988.2, \"fmax_mhz\": 57.689, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4374140, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 4151, \"ff\": 1718, \"seeds\": [56.566, 57.689, 57.689], \"perturbations\": [[0, 56.566, 18], [1, 57.689, 21], [2, 57.689, 21]], \"lutram\": 0, \"bsram\": 4, \"dsp\": 4, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_ex/reg_q.rd_4_s0\", \"to\": \"dmem_1_dmem_1_0_0_s\", \"slack_ns\": -12.678, \"arrival_ns\": 22.973, \"logic_cells\": 18, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 18, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T01:36:19.918133Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 13, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-10-01 hyp-20261001-001-r13s0 (regression, -13.31%): Explicit per-bit generate/propagate terms and expanded block-carry equations around byte-sized `+` operators made the four-block lookahead ADD regress, showing that hand-written carry logic can map worse than an inferred FPGA adder even when it shortens local carry chains.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
