{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260930-001-r3s0.yaml'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260930-001-r3s0\ntitle: \"Share signed and unsigned branch comparison\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The strongest remaining timing risk is the EX branch-resolution path: forwarded operands pass through branch comparison and redirect control before hazards flush the younger pipeline stages. The current branch case expresses signed and unsigned less-than and greater-or-equal comparisons separately, which can infer parallel wide comparators and a result mux.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace the separate signed and unsigned relational branch expressions with one 32-bit unsigned comparator. For signed branches, invert each operand's sign bit before comparison, which maps signed ordering onto unsigned ordering; use the branch funct polarity to choose less-than versus greater-or-equal. Keep a separate equality test for BEQ/BNE. This should reduce duplicated comparator logic and shorten the forwarded-operand-to-redirect path while preserving branch semantics and the existing pipeline and stall behavior.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 7\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Share one sign-adjusted 32-bit ordering comparator across BLT, BGE, BLTU, and BGEU branch resolution.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
