{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"jq 'select(.id == \\\"hyp-20260930-002-r3s1\\\") | {motivation, hypothesis, expected_impact, critical_path, implementation_notes}' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"motivation\": \"The current worst path runs from EX forwarding through redirect and fetch control into the ID register-file read and operand capture. The combinational fetch-to-decode connection lets EX control affect a long path across several pipeline blocks. A registered IF/ID boundary can isolate fetch and decode timing while keeping one instruction per cycle after the pipeline fills.\\n\",\n  \"hypothesis\": {\n    \"motivation\": \"The current worst path runs from EX forwarding through redirect and fetch control into the ID register-file read and operand capture. The combinational fetch-to-decode connection lets EX control affect a long path across several pipeline blocks. A registered IF/ID boundary can isolate fetch and decode timing while keeping one instruction per cycle after the pipeline fills.\\n\",\n    \"hypothesis\": \"Add an explicit IF/ID register between the instruction-memory interface and decode. Hold it with the existing pipeline interlocks, invalidate it on an unserviced fetch, and flush it on redirects. During an EX redirect, drive the instruction-memory address with the redirect target so the target instruction can be captured at that same edge. This moves the EX-to-fetch-to-register-file chain across a register boundary without adding a redirect bubble, and should improve Fmax on the measured cross-stage path.\\n\",\n    \"expected_impact\": {\n      \"fitness_delta_pct\": 7,\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    \"changes\": [\n      {\n        \"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\",\n        \"description\": \"Add a registered IF/ID payload, separate its hold and invalidation conditions, and issue redirect-target fetches early enough to capture at the redirect edge.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\",\n        \"description\": \"Connect fetch readiness and pipeline hold control to the registered IF/ID boundary while preserving the existing core and RVFI interfaces.\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"expected_impact\": {\n    \"fitness_delta_pct\": 7,\n    \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  \"critical_path\": {\n    \"from\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.rs1_addr_0_s0\",\n    \"to\": \"dmem_1_dmem_1_0_0_s\",\n    \"slack_ns\": -15.461,\n    \"arrival_ns\": 25.756,\n    \"logic_cells\": 19,\n    \"modules\": [\n      \"clock_ibuf\",\n      \"cpu/u_fwd\",\n      \"cpu/u_ex\",\n      \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\",\n      \"cpu/u_ex\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"implementation_notes\": \"\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
