{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"The best path is still dominated by EX forwarding and branch redirect feedback into decode. I’m proposing a narrow change to bubble injection in ID: keep datapath fields flowing and zero only validity/control on a bubble, which removes redirect/load-use flush from the wide ID/EX payload muxes while preserving side-effect suppression."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"mkdir -p cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses && cat > cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260930-001-r6s0.yaml <<'EOF'\nid: hyp-20260930-001-r6s0\ntitle: \\\"Narrow ID bubble gating\\\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The best design's critical paths still pass through EX forwarding and redirect logic into the decode pipeline. ID currently uses flush to clear every ID/EX field, so redirect and load-use control drives a wide bank of payload muxes. Narrowing bubble control can reduce that fanout and ease routing on the timed EX-to-ID path.\nhypothesis: |\n  Change ID/EX bubble injection so a flush captures the ordinary datapath payload but forces valid low and clears the decoded control bundle. Reset still clears the full register, and a non-flushed stall still holds it. Clearing controls prevents an invalid load/store, branch, jump, or register write from causing side effects, while valid remains the retirement guard. This should remove redirect/load-use flush from wide data-field muxes and improve Fmax without adding state or changing pipeline latency.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \\\"Limit flush-controlled bubble injection to the valid bit and control bundle while allowing datapath fields to capture normally; preserve full reset clearing and stall holds.\\\"\nEOF\npython3 -c 'import yaml; p=\\\"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260930-001-r6s0.yaml\\\"; d=yaml.safe_load(open(p)); print(d[\\\"id\\\"], d[\\\"category\\\"], d[\\\"expected_impact\\\"], len(d[\\\"changes\\\"]))'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
