{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cat > cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260930-002-r6s1.yaml <<'EOF'\nid: hyp-20260930-002-r6s1\ntitle: \\\"Resolve conditional branches in decode\\\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  Recent critical paths repeatedly cross forwarding, EX, and fetch control before reaching decode and register-file logic. Conditional branch comparison and target generation in EX put branch control on this long path. Resolving conditional branches in decode can remove that work from the EX redirect cone and let the fetch PC redirect directly from the branch instruction being decoded.\nhypothesis: |\n  Move conditional branch operand comparison and target calculation into ID, and issue the redirect in the same cycle the branch is decoded. Add decode-stage bypasses for values already available from EX/MEM and MEM/WB, and interlock a branch until a preceding load or unavailable EX result can be supplied correctly. Carry the resolved branch outcome and target with the branch through EX/MEM so RVFI pc_wdata remains exact; allow the branch itself to advance while discarding only the younger wrong-path fetch. This should shorten the recurring EX-to-fetch control path, with a small cost in branch dependency stalls.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 7\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: Add pipeline metadata for the decode-resolved branch outcome and target through retirement.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: Route decode-stage branch redirects and operand bypass candidates to fetch and decode control.\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: Compare forwarded branch operands, calculate the branch target, and pass resolved metadata with the branch.\n  - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n    description: Provide priority-correct decode-stage branch bypass selection from available pipeline results.\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: Interlock decode-stage branches when operand data is not yet available and arbitrate branch issue with bus stalls.\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: Redirect the PC from an issued decode-stage branch while suppressing only the younger fetched instruction.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: Consume resolved branch metadata for retirement and prevent conditional branches from resolving twice in EX.\nEOF\ncat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260930-002-r6s1.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
