{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cat > cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260930-003-r2s2.yaml <<'EOF'\nid: hyp-20260930-003-r2s2\ntitle: \\\"Direct mapped branch target predictor\\\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The previous static predictor added instruction decode and a branch target adder to fetch, hurting timing more than its loop prediction helped. CoreMark revisits loop branches often, so recording resolved branch targets and outcomes should still remove recurring redirect bubbles without rebuilding the target from the fetched instruction.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a small direct-mapped branch target buffer indexed by fetch PC, with a PC tag, saved target, and 2-bit saturating direction counter. On a tagged hit predicted taken, fetch the saved target; train the entry when a conditional branch resolves in EX. Carry the prediction with the instruction and redirect only when EX finds the outcome or target was mispredicted. This trades a small table lookup for the existing branch bubbles while keeping branch-immediate decode and target addition out of the fetch path; repeated loop branches should improve CoreMark IPC with less timing cost than static backward-taken prediction.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: Add branch prediction metadata to the fetch/decode and ID/EX pipeline bundles.\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: Look up the current PC in a small tagged target table and select a saved target on a predicted-taken hit.\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: Carry the fetch prediction alongside the decoded branch into EX.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: Compare prediction with resolved branch outcome and target, and provide branch resolution updates for the predictor.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: Connect predictor lookup and EX resolution updates while preserving stall, redirect, and retirement handling.\nEOF\n\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
