{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_6", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n -i 'predict|branch|btb|ras|retim' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "4:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260930-003-r1s2\", \"title\": \"Predict backward branches taken at fetch\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"Conditional branches currently resolve in EX, so a taken branch flushes younger work and redirects fetch after a two-instruction penalty. CoreMark contains frequent backward loop branches, which are commonly taken and account for repeated avoidable bubbles.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"Conditional branches currently resolve in EX, so a taken branch flushes younger work and redirects fetch after a two-instruction penalty. CoreMark contains frequent backward loop branches, which are commonly taken and account for repeated avoidable bubbles.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a static backward-taken predictor in IF: recognize conditional branch instructions from the fetched instruction, form their B-immediate target, and advance the PC to that target when the branch is backward. Carry the predicted next PC with the instruction and compare it against the resolved next PC in EX; preserve the existing redirect and flush behavior only on a mismatch. Correct loop predictions then avoid branch bubbles while forward branches retain the existing not-taken behavior. The fetch-side instruction decode and target adder may affect Fmax, so the expected net gain is moderate.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add predicted-next-PC metadata to the fetch/decode and ID/EX pipeline bundles.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Detect backward conditional branches, calculate their target, and select it as the sequential PC when predicted taken.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Carry prediction metadata from the fetched branch into ID/EX for comparison during resolution.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compare actual and predicted next PCs, redirecting and flushing only when prediction is incorrect.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Connect prediction metadata and retain load/da\n…[23055 of 26127 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:6ffc6d1c3312238d]…\n6.62, \"vs_baseline\": 572.11, \"fmax_mhz\": 34.708, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4260805, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 4283, \"ff\": 1703, \"seeds\": [35.493, 34.708, 34.708], \"perturbations\": [[0, 35.493, 31], [1, 34.708, 30], [2, 34.708, 30]], \"lutram\": 22, \"bsram\": 4, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_mem/reg_q.rd_2_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.rs1_val_20_s0\", \"slack_ns\": -23.175, \"arrival_ns\": 33.469, \"logic_cells\": 69, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_fwd\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_if\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_if\", \"cpu/u_rf\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 31, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-30T21:38:01.336031Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 5, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-09-30 hyp-20260930-003-r5s2 (regression, -26.62%): Retiming a 16-entry BTB lookup still leaves indexed tag and target reads from `next_pc` into prediction registers, while the full table adds state, so moving the result register alone did not offset its fetch cost with saved CoreMark redirects.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
