{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260930-003-r6s2.yaml'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260930-003-r6s2\ntitle: \"Tagless indexed branch target predictor\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  EX-resolved taken branches cost fetch bubbles, while prior predictor variants reduced Fmax by putting full PC tag comparisons, target selection, or instruction immediate addition on the fetch path. A direct-indexed target table can retain learned targets and direction state while eliminating the wide tag compare that burdened the single-entry BTB.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a modest direct-indexed branch target table using a subset of aligned PC bits, with each entry holding a target and a saturating direction counter but no full-PC tag. Fetch consults the indexed entry only for conditional branch instructions; a predicted-taken entry supplies its previously learned target. EX trains the selected entry and retains redirect recovery on misses and incorrect predictions, so index aliases can affect performance but not architectural correctness. This removes tag-compare logic from the fetch path and gives repeatedly executed CoreMark loop branches a chance to avoid EX redirect bubbles with less timing overhead than tagged BTBs.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 7\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Carry predicted-taken state and prediction target with the fetched instruction through the pipeline.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Add a compact PC-indexed target and direction table, using its target on predicted-taken branch entries without a full-PC tag comparison.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Preserve the fetch prediction metadata through ID/EX.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Train the indexed entry from resolved conditional branches and redirect on prediction mismatch.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Connect table training and prediction metadata while retaining existing stalls, flushes, and retirement behavior.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
