anch comparison\tregression\t-1.13\tcpu/u_mem/reg_q.rd_3_s0\tcpu/u_id/reg_q.rs2_val_13_s0\tclock_ibuf > cpu/u_fwd > cpu/u_ex > cpu/u_if > cpu/u_rf\tReplace the separate signed and unsigned relational branch expressions with one 32-bit unsigned comparator. For signed branches, invert each operand's sign bit before comparison, which maps signed ordering onto unsigned ordering; use the branch funct polarity to choose less-than versus greater-or-equal. Keep a separate equality test for BEQ/BNE. This should reduce duplicated comp\n…[6062 of 9134 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:71cdb6690923f306]…\nr byte, sums for both possible carry-ins in parallel; use per-block generate/propagate signals to select each byte and carry. This limits serial carry work to byte-sized adders and a small block carry network while preserving the existing ALU operation selection, forwarding timing, branch comparisons, and all non-ADD results. The added parallel sums may cost LUTs, but the current design has substantial area headroom. \nhyp-20261001-001-r13s0\tBlock carry-lookahead ALU addition\tregression\t-13.31\tcpu/u_ex/reg_q.rd_4_s0\tdmem_1_dmem_1_0_0_s\tclock_ibuf > cpu/u_ex > cpu/u_ex/u_alu > cpu/u_ex\tReplace the ALU's full-width ADD implementation with four 8-bit sum blocks. Compute each block's generate and propagate terms and derive the carries between blocks with parallel lookahead equations, while each block performs only a short local addition. Keep operation selection, operands, and all other ALU results unchanged. This targets the common 32-bit add path without adding pipeline latency or changing dependency behavior. \n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
