{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261001-001-r14s0.yaml'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261001-001-r14s0\ntitle: \"Register MEM/WB forwarding eligibility\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The recent timing path starts at the MEM/WB destination and runs through forwarding, EX branch resolution, and IF PC selection. Forwarding still qualifies the MEM/WB match with live write-enable and rd-zero checks, leaving control logic on this path.\nhypothesis: |\n  Capture a single MEM/WB forwarding-eligibility bit alongside the pipeline entry, combining the final trap-adjusted register-write control with rd != x0. Use that bit to qualify the already registered source-match metadata in the forwarding unit, removing the live destination-zero comparison and write-enable decode from the WB bypass select. Retain this bit when MEM/WB is held during a data stall so dependent instructions can still forward the held load result. This should shorten the reported MEM/WB-to-EX-to-PC path without changing instruction timing or forwarding priority.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add a registered forwarding-eligibility field to the MEM/WB pipeline bundle.\"\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: \"Capture final trap-adjusted reg-write eligibility and rd != x0, retaining it across held MEM/WB cycles.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Connect the registered MEM/WB eligibility bit to the forwarding unit.\"\n  - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n    description: \"Use the prequalified MEM/WB eligibility bit with the existing source match and EX/MEM priority.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
