risons and operand selection before reaching the EX ALU and memory interface. Registering the register-match decisions alongside the instruction can remove the equality comparators from this cycle's path.\nhypothesis: |\n  Compare each fetched instruction's source registers in ID against the destinations that will occupy EX/MEM and MEM/WB in the following execute cycle, and capture those match bits with the ID/EX payload. Use the registered matches to select the youngest live producer in EX, retaining dynamic write-enable qualification, EX/MEM priority, zero-register handling, and the existing operand values as fallback. Hold and flush the metadata with its instruction so stalls, redirects, and bubbles preserve alignment. This should shorten the currently measured forwarding-to-ALU path without adding work to the fetch PC path.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add EX/MEM and MEM/WB source-match metadata to the ID/EX payload.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Compute source-to-producer destination matches in ID and capture them with the instruction.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Connect the ID/EX and EX/MEM destination metadata needed for early match generation.\"\n  - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n    description: \"Select forwarded operands from registered match bits while retaining producer enables and priority.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Use the registered forwarding matches for both EX operand muxes.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
