{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cat > cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261001-002-r11s1.yaml <<'YAML'\nid: hyp-20261001-002-r11s1\ntitle: \\\"Register operands before execute\\\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The recent FPGA timing paths still cross the execute stage's operand and arithmetic logic before reaching a memory-side output. Forwarding selection, ALU work, and branch resolution currently share one cycle. A pipeline boundary after forwarded operand preparation can reduce the combinational work on this path while preserving one-instruction-per-cycle throughput.\nhypothesis: |\n  Split execute into an operand-preparation stage and an arithmetic stage. The first stage selects the freshest forwarded source values and registers them with the instruction, PC, immediate, and control metadata; the second stage performs ALU/address generation and branch or jump resolution into EX/MEM. Add a dedicated younger-entry flush on redirects and align IF, both execute-stage valid bits, and PC-next metadata so no wrong-path instruction retires and consecutive retirement PCs remain continuous. Keep load-use, data-memory stall, divider, and multiplier interlocks aligned to the new boundary. With forwarding selection no longer serial with the ALU, the common register-to-result path should shorten; the existing direction predictor should limit the added branch-resolution cost.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 7\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \\\"Add an operand-stage payload carrying forwarded values and the instruction metadata needed by execute and retirement.\\\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \\\"Register forwarded operands before arithmetic, then resolve ALU operations and control flow in a separate stage while preserving one-time M-unit completion.\\\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \\\"Wire the added execute boundary without changing top-level IO or the single-channel RVFI contract.\\\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \\\"Align data, redirect, memory, divide, and multiply interlocks and younger-stage flushing with the added execute stage.\\\"\nYAML\n\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
