pu/u_ex/u_multiplier/pp_hl_31_s1 => dmem_3_dmem_3_0_0_s arrival 18.702 cells 13 notes \nhyp-20261001-003-r11s2 Expand the loop direction predictor regression delta -5.61 score 143.61 mhz 62.425 ipc 2e-06 path cpu/u_mem/reg_q.rd_3_s0 => dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s arrival 20.583 cells 14 notes \n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 -c 'import json; rows=[json.loads(x) for x in open(\\\"cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\\\")]; ids={\\\"hyp-20260930-002-r5s1\\\",\\\"hyp-20261001-001-r8s0\\\",\\\"hyp-20261001-003-r10s2\\\"};\nfor r in rows:\n if r.get(\\\"id\\\") in ids:\n  print(\\\"\\\\n\\\",r[\\\"id\\\"],r[\\\"title\\\"],r.get(\\\"delta_pct\\\")); print(r.get(\\\"hypothesis\\\",{}).get(\\\"hypothesis\\\",r.get(\\\"hypothesis\\\"))); print(r.get(\\\"changes\\\")); print(r.get(\\\"critical_path\\\"))'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_8", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 -c 'import json; rows=[json.loads(x) for x in open(\\\"cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\\\")]; ids={\\\"hyp-20260930-002-r5s1\\\",\\\"hyp-20261001-001-r8s0\\\",\\\"hyp-20261001-003-r10s2\\\"};\nfor r in rows:\n if r.get(\\\"id\\\") in ids:\n  print(\\\"\\\\n\\\",r[\\\"id\\\"],r[\\\"title\\\"],r.get(\\\"delta_pct\\\")); print(r.get(\\\"hypothesis\\\",{}).get(\\\"hypothesis\\\",r.get(\\\"hypothesis\\\"))); print(r.get(\\\"changes\\\")); print(r.get(\\\"critical_path\\\"))'\"", "aggregated_output": "\n hyp-20260930-002-r5s1 Parallel speculative address generation -1.75\nAdd a dedicated EX address-generation path that computes the effective address in parallel for the ID/EX rs1 value, the EX/MEM result, and the MEM/WB writeback value. Select among the completed sums using the existing priority-correct forwarding select, then use that address for load/store outputs and the EX/MEM address field. Moving forwarding selection after the adder should remove the register comparison and operand mux from the address carry path, improving Fmax while leaving instruction timing and bus handshakes unchanged. Preserve misalignment trapping, memory masks, and all existing stall behavior.\n\n[{'file': 'rtl/ex_stage.sv', 'description': 'Compute load/store effective addresses for all three possible forwarded rs1 values in parallel, then select the completed address late and route it to EX/MEM.'}]\n{'from': 'cpu/u_mem/reg_q.rd_3_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_id/reg_q.rs2_val_28_s0', 'slack_ns': -15.273, 'arrival_ns': 25.567, 'logic_cells': 48, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_fwd', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_if', 'cpu/u_rf']}\n\n hyp-20261001-001-r8s0 Dedicated memory address adder 5.8\nCompute the effective address directly in EX as forwarded rs1 plus the decoded immediate, and capture that sum as the EX/MEM result for loads and stores. Keep the general ALU path for other operations and preserve the existing MEM-stage alignment checks, byte-lane logic, forwarding priority, and RVFI reporting. This specializes the timed dmem address path and may remove general ALU result-selection logic from its critical cone.\n\n[{'file': 'rtl/ex_stage.sv', 'description': 'Add a dedicated forwarded-rs1 plus immediate effective-address sum and use it for load/store results captured into EX/MEM.'}]\n{'from': 'cpu/u_ex/reg_q.rd_3_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/reg_q.alu_result_12_s0', 'slack_ns': -12.63, 'arrival_ns': 22.924, 'logic_cells': 14, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_fwd', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']}\n\n hyp-20261001-003-r10s2 Direction-only loop branch predictor 4.85\nAdd a small PC-indexed table of 2-bit saturating direction counters, initialized weakly not-taken. During fetch, use the current instruction's branch immediate to form a target only for a predicted-taken conditional branch, and carry the direction and target prediction with the instruction. Train the counter when the branch resolves in EX, and retain precise redirect recovery whenever the resolved next PC differs from the prediction. This learns taken loop iterations and not-taken exits while removing BTB target storage and lookup muxing, improving CoreMark iterations per cycle with less predictor state and fetch lookup logic.\n\n[{'file': 'rtl/core_pkg.sv', 'description': 'Add direction prediction metadata to the fetch and ID/EX pipeline records.'}, {'file': 'rtl/if_stage.sv', 'description': \"Read a small PC-indexed direction table and select the instruction's immediate target only for predicted-taken branches.\"}, {'file': 'rtl/id_stage.sv', 'description': 'Carry branch prediction metadata with the decoded instruction into EX.'}, {'file': 'rtl/ex_stage.sv', 'description': 'Train direction counters from resolved branches and correct the fetch PC on prediction mismatches.'}, {'file': 'rtl/core.sv', 'description': 'Connect predictor lookup and update signals while preserving stall, flush, and retirement behavior.'}]\n{'from': 'cpu/u_ex/reg_q.rd_3_s0', 'to': 'dmem_2_dmem_2_0_0_s', 'slack_ns': -10.482, 'arrival_ns': 20.777, 'logic_cells': 14, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
