{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"git status --short -- cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261001-002-r13s1.yaml && sed -n '1,80p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261001-002-r13s1.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261001-002-r13s1\ntitle: \"Bank the register file in synchronous RAM\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The explicit two-read register file builds a large asynchronous selection network from 32 words, adding LUT and routing pressure to a small FPGA. Even though recent worst paths are in EX forwarding and arithmetic, that network consumes placement resources and can constrain the physical implementation of the critical EX cone.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replicate the register-file storage into two write-mirrored FPGA RAM banks, one synchronous read port per source operand, and add an IF/ID boundary that keeps each instruction aligned with its registered read results. Preserve one-instruction-per-cycle steady-state flow, x0 behavior, reset-visible zero values through per-register validity bits, same-cycle WB write-through, and existing stall/redirect semantics. Replacing the wide asynchronous LUT read network with compact RAM reads should free logic and routing resources for EX placement and may improve Fmax without adding steady-state CoreMark cycles.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/reg_file.sv\n    description: \"Replace asynchronous one-hot register reads with two write-mirrored synchronous RAM banks, per-register validity, and aligned write-through bypass.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Add a held and flushable fetch/decode register so instruction metadata aligns with synchronous register-file read data.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Align decode and ID/EX capture with the registered source operands while retaining hazard and forwarding metadata correctness.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Coordinate the added fetch/decode boundary with existing interlocks, redirects, and memory stalls without changing the top-level interface.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
