avior, and retain the ALTOPS formal stand-ins under RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS. This should shorten the DSP arithmetic path at the cost of one extra execute cycle per multiply.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: \"Remove the combinational RV32M multiply cones and select the completed pipelined result for MUL and high-half variants, retaining ALTOPS substitutions.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Add multiply start, wait, and consume control; hold the in-flight instruction until the partial-product pipeline completes and then send it to EX/MEM once.\"\n  - file: rtl/iterative_multiplier.sv\n    description: \"Implement a two-stage 32-by-32 multiplier using registered 16-by-16 partial products and signed high-half corrections.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Integrate the multiply wait with redirect, divider, load-use, and memory-backpressure interlocks.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Connect the EX multiply interlock to pipeline control while preserving in-order retirement and bus handshakes.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
